fix(ai): sanitize request URLs before telemetry observes provider results (#24708)

## Background

Provider request URLs were sanitized only after
`executeLanguageModelCall` returned. Telemetry integrations and Node
tracing-channel `asyncEnd` subscribers could therefore observe
credentials and other sensitive endpoint components before public
results were reduced to the origin. The issue applies to `main` at
7772d0ca0f7abc2cb2a0ad61b0272a72655d780d.

## Summary

- Sanitize request metadata inside the `generateText` and streaming
provider execution callbacks, before results reach telemetry wrappers.
- Preserve request bodies, optional metadata, provider-owned objects,
and existing public result behavior across providers.
- Add regression coverage for both APIs, including immediate
subscriber/integration observations, credential-bearing URLs,
invalid/non-HTTP URLs, and missing endpoint/request metadata.
- Inline the unchanged response metadata construction and simplify the
optional request spread to fit the existing bundle-size cap.
- Add an `ai` patch changeset. No provider interfaces, dependencies, or
public APIs change.

## End-to-End Verification

The same standalone script exercises `generateText` and `streamText`
through the real OpenAI Chat provider and a local HTTP endpoint, using
rebuilt workspace packages before and after the fix. It checks URL
sanitization when telemetry integrations and Node tracing subscribers
receive the provider result, and when the application receives its
result.

<details>
<summary>Reproduction code, setup, and before/after results</summary>

Prerequisites: supported Node.js (this run used v26.13.0), pnpm 12.14.0,
installed workspace dependencies, and permission to bind an ephemeral
loopback port. No external credentials or services are required. All
endpoint and API-key credentials in this script are synthetic. Save the
complete script outside the checkout as
`/tmp/ai-sdk-tracing-url-fix/repro.mjs`:

```js
import { createServer } from 'node:http';
import { once } from 'node:events';
import { tracingChannel } from 'node:diagnostics_channel';
import { createOpenAI } from '@ai-sdk/openai';
import { generateText, streamText } from 'ai';

console.log('local packages', import.meta.resolve('ai'), import.meta.resolve('@ai-sdk/openai'));
const server = createServer(async (request, response) => {
  let body = '';
  for await (const chunk of request) body += chunk;
  const { stream } = JSON.parse(body);
  const completion = {
    id: 'local-completion', object: 'chat.completion', created: 0,
    model: 'local-model',
    choices: [{ index: 0, message: { role: 'assistant', content: 'Hello' }, finish_reason: 'stop' }],
    usage: { prompt_tokens: 1, completion_tokens: 1, total_tokens: 2 },
  };
  if (stream) {
    response.writeHead(200, { 'content-type': 'text/event-stream' });
    response.end(`data: ${JSON.stringify({
      id: 'local-completion', object: 'chat.completion.chunk', created: 0,
      model: 'local-model',
      choices: [{ index: 0, delta: { role: 'assistant', content: 'Hello' }, finish_reason: 'stop' }],
      usage: completion.usage,
    })}\n\ndata: [DONE]\n\n`);
  } else {
    response.writeHead(200, { 'content-type': 'application/json' });
    response.end(JSON.stringify(completion));
  }
});
server.listen(0, '127.0.0.1');
await once(server, 'listening');
const origin = `http://127.0.0.1:${server.address().port}`;
const model = createOpenAI({
  apiKey: 'local-test-only',
  baseURL: `${origin}/endpoint-credential/v1?api_key=query-credential`,
}).chat('local-model');
const channel = tracingChannel('ai:telemetry');
let activeApi;
const subscribers = {
  start() {}, end() {}, asyncStart() {}, error() {},
  asyncEnd(message) {
    if (message.type === 'languageModelCall') {
      console.log(activeApi, 'tracing subscriber', {
        urlSanitized: message.result?.request?.url === origin,
      });
    }
  },
};
channel.subscribe(subscribers);
try {
  for (const api of ['generateText', 'streamText']) {
    activeApi = api;
    const options = {
      model, prompt: 'Hello', maxRetries: 0,
      telemetry: { integrations: [{
        async executeLanguageModelCall({ execute }) {
          const result = await execute();
          console.log(api, 'telemetry integration', {
            urlSanitized: result.request?.url === origin,
          });
          return result;
        },
      }] },
    };
    const result = api === 'generateText'
      ? await generateText(options)
      : streamText(options);
    console.log(api, 'public result', {
      text: await result.text,
      urlSanitized: (await result.finalStep).request.url === origin,
    });
  }
} finally {
  channel.unsubscribe(subscribers);
  server.closeAllConnections();
  await new Promise(resolve => server.close(resolve));
}
```

Run the following from each clean checkout, first at the base commit
`7772d0ca0f7abc2cb2a0ad61b0272a72655d780d`, then at the final fix commit
`dcbd1712fbe9e83fdde07585442f04eae1e8ec1b`:

```sh
pnpm install --frozen-lockfile
pnpm exec turbo build --filter=ai... --filter=@ai-sdk/openai...
cd examples/ai-functions
node --input-type=module < /tmp/ai-sdk-tracing-url-fix/repro.mjs
```

The actual before and after runs used
`/Users/gr2m/.codex/worktrees/51f7/ai`, first at the base before
production edits and then with the fix. `import.meta.resolve` confirms
that both packages resolve to this checkout's `packages/*/dist/index.js`
through workspace links. The build command was run separately before
each public API run.

Before:

```text
local packages file:///Users/gr2m/.codex/worktrees/51f7/ai/packages/ai/dist/index.js file:///Users/gr2m/.codex/worktrees/51f7/ai/packages/openai/dist/index.js
generateText telemetry integration { urlSanitized: false }
generateText tracing subscriber { urlSanitized: false }
generateText public result { text: 'Hello', urlSanitized: true }
streamText telemetry integration { urlSanitized: false }
streamText tracing subscriber { urlSanitized: false }
streamText public result { text: 'Hello', urlSanitized: true }
```

After:

```text
local packages file:///Users/gr2m/.codex/worktrees/51f7/ai/packages/ai/dist/index.js file:///Users/gr2m/.codex/worktrees/51f7/ai/packages/openai/dist/index.js
generateText telemetry integration { urlSanitized: true }
generateText tracing subscriber { urlSanitized: true }
generateText public result { text: 'Hello', urlSanitized: true }
streamText telemetry integration { urlSanitized: true }
streamText tracing subscriber { urlSanitized: true }
streamText public result { text: 'Hello', urlSanitized: true }
```

Both APIs previously exposed the full endpoint to the integration and
tracing subscriber (`urlSanitized: false`) while sanitizing the public
result. With the fix all six observations report `urlSanitized: true`,
and generated text remains `Hello`.

Limits: this is a deterministic local HTTP application flow using the
shipped OpenAI provider, not a live OpenAI inference call. No production
endpoint or credential was contacted or exposed. The loopback flow
verifies the request/result/tracing boundary; it does not validate
remote inference or unrelated provider behavior. An initial sandboxed
attempt could not bind the loopback port (`EPERM`); both successful runs
used the permitted local server execution.

</details>

## Validation

- Before the fix: the focused regression matrix failed in six
sensitive-URL cases and passed four metadata-compatibility cases.
- After the fix: focused Node and Edge suites each passed 855 tests,
with 3 existing skips and no type errors.
- `pnpm check`: passed.
- `pnpm discover-guidelines --modified` and `pnpm run-verifiers
--modified`: no applicable guidelines/verifiers.
- `pnpm type-check:full`: passed again after the final production
changes.
- Claude Code Opus 5.5 (`claude-opus-5-5`, confirmed by canonical model
metadata): two successful read-only reviews, including the complete
final diff at `dcbd1712fbe9e83fdde07585442f04eae1e8ec1b`, found no
actionable issues in the task diff. Both completed without tool
permission denials. No review-fix commits were needed; the CI bundle
repair is a separate signed commit.
- `pnpm --filter ai check-bundle-size`: passed with all existing limits.
The named Node `generateText` bundle is 302078 bytes against a
302080-byte cap (2 bytes of headroom). The unchanged base was 302069
bytes.
- CI: all 57 checks passed on final head
`dcbd1712fbe9e83fdde07585442f04eae1e8ec1b`, including every required
check. The complete CI workflow and changeset verification succeeded.
Both commits are signed and verified by GitHub.

## Checklist

- [x] All commits are signed (PRs with unsigned commits cannot be
merged)
- [x] Tests have been added / updated (for bug fixes / features)
- [ ] Documentation has been added / updated (for bug fixes / features)
- [x] A _patch_ changeset for relevant packages has been added (for bug
fixes / features - run `pnpm changeset` in the project root)
- [x] I have reviewed this pull request (self-review)

Documentation is unchanged because no public API or configuration
changes.

## Future Work

The independent review noted a similar pre-existing issue in the
separate `WorkflowAgent` provider execution path
(`packages/workflow/src/do-generate-step.ts:133-146`, connected to the
core dispatcher by
`packages/workflow/src/model-call-telemetry.ts:141-142`). That path does
not call `generateText` or `streamText` and is outside this PR's scope.
A follow-up should sanitize its request metadata before its telemetry
execution callback returns, and assess its included request metadata.
This PR fixes the two text-generation paths in the supplied report.

