test(examples): cover concurrent MCP OAuth requests (#24693)

## Background

Concurrent OAuth requests in the old Next.js MCP example opened
competing listeners on port 8090 and could terminate Node with an
unhandled `EADDRINUSE`. Merged PR #24690 already replaces that listener
with the application callback route, session isolation, and five-minute
consent expiry. The v5 release branch is also protected by #24401.

This PR adds regression coverage for that existing fix; it does not
change application or SDK behavior.

## Summary

- Add eight route tests for anonymous requests, concurrent sessions,
overlapping requests, consent reuse, five-minute expiry, callback
correlation, single-use callbacks, and cleanup after denial.
- Add the `test:mcp-auth` command already referenced by the example
README.
- Run these tests in CI after workspace packages are built.

## End-to-End Verification

Checked the actual local Next.js HTTP route with concurrent anonymous
requests. A separate before/after integration check invokes the route
with rebuilt local SDK packages and a substituted authorization function
to exercise concurrent pending consent without contacting third-party
systems.

<details>
<summary>Reproduction code, setup, before/after results, and
limits</summary>

Prerequisites: Node.js 26.13.0, pnpm 12.14.0, the repository
dependencies (`pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`), and a free local
callback port 8090 for the old route. No credentials are required. Run
from the checkout root. Save this single reproduction outside the
checkout as `/tmp/reproduce-mcp-oauth.mjs`.

```js
import { spawnSync, execFileSync } from 'node:child_process';
import { createRequire, registerHooks } from 'node:module';
import { readFileSync, writeFileSync, mkdtempSync, symlinkSync, existsSync, realpathSync } from 'node:fs';
import { tmpdir } from 'node:os';
import { join } from 'node:path';
import { pathToFileURL, fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';

// Run from the checkout root. Only auth() is replaced; no network calls occur.
const checkout = process.cwd();
const example = join(checkout, 'examples/ai-e2e-next');
const routePath = 'examples/ai-e2e-next/app/api/chat/mcp-with-auth/route.ts';
if (process.argv[2] !== 'child') {
  const directory = mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), 'mcp-callback-'));
  symlinkSync(join(example, 'node_modules'), join(directory, 'node_modules'));
  const ref = process.env.OAUTH_ROUTE_REF;
  const source = ref
    ? execFileSync('git', ['show', `${ref}:${routePath}`], { encoding: 'utf8' })
    : readFileSync(join(checkout, routePath), 'utf8');
  writeFileSync(join(directory, 'route.ts'), source);
  writeFileSync(join(directory, 'oauth-stub.mjs'), `
    export async function auth(provider) {
      const state = await provider.state?.();
      if (state) await provider.saveState(state);
      await provider.saveCodeVerifier('local-verifier');
      const url = new URL('https://authorization.example/authorize');
      url.searchParams.set('redirect_uri', String(provider.redirectUrl));
      if (state) url.searchParams.set('state', state);
      await provider.redirectToAuthorization(url);
      return 'REDIRECT';
    }
    export function createMCPClient() { throw new Error('Unexpected MCP connection'); }
  `);
  const require = createRequire(join(example, 'package.json'));
  console.log('ai:', require.resolve('ai'));
  console.log('mcp (replaced in this isolated check):', require.resolve('@ai-sdk/mcp'));
  console.log('route:', ref ?? execFileSync('git', ['rev-parse', 'HEAD'], { encoding: 'utf8' }).trim());
  const result = spawnSync(process.execPath, [fileURLToPath(import.meta.url), 'child', directory, ref ? 'before' : 'after'], {
    encoding: 'utf8', timeout: 10000,
    env: { ...process.env, NODE_ENV: 'development', VERCEL: undefined },
  });
  console.log(result.stdout);
  console.log(result.stderr);
  console.log('Child exit:', result.status, 'signal:', result.signal);
} else {
  const directory = process.argv[3];
  const before = process.argv[4] === 'before';
  const require = createRequire(join(checkout, 'package.json'));
  const ts = require('typescript');
  registerHooks({
    resolve(specifier, context, nextResolve) {
      if (specifier === '@ai-sdk/mcp') {
        return nextResolve(pathToFileURL(join(directory, 'oauth-stub.mjs')).href, context);
      }
      if (specifier.startsWith('.')) {
        const parent = context.parentURL?.startsWith('file:') && realpathSync(fileURLToPath(context.parentURL)) === realpathSync(join(directory, 'route.ts'))
          ? pathToFileURL(join(checkout, routePath)).href
          : context.parentURL;
        const candidate = fileURLToPath(new URL(specifier, parent));
        if (existsSync(candidate + '.ts')) {
          return nextResolve(pathToFileURL(candidate + '.ts').href, context);
        }
      }
      return nextResolve(specifier, context);
    },
    load(url, context, nextLoad) {
      if (url.endsWith('.ts')) {
        return { format: 'module', shortCircuit: true, source: ts.transpileModule(readFileSync(fileURLToPath(url), 'utf8'), {
          compilerOptions: { module: ts.ModuleKind.ESNext, target: ts.ScriptTarget.ES2022 },
        }).outputText };
      }
      return nextLoad(url, context);
    },
  });
  const route = await import(pathToFileURL(join(directory, 'route.ts')).href);
  const url = 'http://localhost:3000/api/chat/mcp-with-auth';
  const request = (cookie = '', method = 'GET') => new Request(url, {
    method, headers: { host: 'localhost:3000', origin: 'http://localhost:3000', cookie },
    ...(method === 'POST' ? { body: JSON.stringify({ messages: [] }) } : {}),
  });
  const cookies = before ? ['', ''] : await Promise.all([0, 1].map(async () => {
    const response = await route.GET(request());
    return response.headers.get('set-cookie').split(';')[0];
  }));
  const responses = await Promise.all(cookies.map(cookie => route.POST(request(cookie, 'POST'))));
  console.log('POST statuses:', responses.map(response => response.status));
  const bodies = await Promise.all(responses.map(response => response.text()));
  console.log('Consent responses:', bodies.map(body => body.includes('data-oauth')));
}
```

The SDK packages are unchanged between pre-fix source commit
`f608c056a2c1bf0c9497043302dd9606641c5d03` and fixed application commit
`a6860a687011dbf025388ee419db730e05fb9ce0`. Both runs use this
checkout's rebuilt workspace packages; the script prints their resolved
absolute paths. The old route is loaded from Git into a temporary
directory. The current route's relative helpers load from this checkout.

```sh
# Before: build local packages, then load the original application route.
pnpm exec turbo build --filter=ai... --filter=@ai-sdk/openai... --filter=@ai-sdk/mcp...
OAUTH_ROUTE_REF=f608c056a2c1bf0c9497043302dd9606641c5d03 node /tmp/reproduce-mcp-oauth.mjs

# After: rebuild, then load the current application route.
pnpm exec turbo build --filter=ai... --filter=@ai-sdk/openai... --filter=@ai-sdk/mcp...
node /tmp/reproduce-mcp-oauth.mjs
```

Before output:

```text
ai: /Users/gr2m/.codex/worktrees/375b/ai/packages/ai/dist/index.js
mcp (replaced in this isolated check): /Users/gr2m/.codex/worktrees/375b/ai/packages/mcp/dist/index.js
route: f608c056a2c1bf0c9497043302dd9606641c5d03
POST statuses: [ 200, 200 ]
OAuth callback server: http://localhost:8090/callback

node:events:505
    throw er; // Unhandled 'error' event
    ^

Error: listen EADDRINUSE: address already in use :::8090
    at Server.setupListenHandle [as _listen2] (node:net:2390:16)
    at listenInCluster (node:net:2499:12)
    at Server.listen (node:net:2624:7)
    at file:///private/var/folders/9g/f2ljbzrd2yx0xz_byqrmrmxw0000gn/T/mcp-callback-v5Zqjl/route.ts:134:16
    at new Promise (<anonymous>)
    at waitForAuthorizationCode (file:///private/var/folders/9g/f2ljbzrd2yx0xz_byqrmrmxw0000gn/T/mcp-callback-v5Zqjl/route.ts:107:12)
    at execute (file:///private/var/folders/9g/f2ljbzrd2yx0xz_byqrmrmxw0000gn/T/mcp-callback-v5Zqjl/route.ts:162:53)
    at async file:///Users/gr2m/.codex/worktrees/375b/ai/packages/ai/dist/index.js:11151:44
Emitted 'error' event on Server instance at:
    at emitErrorNT (node:net:2478:8)
    at process.processTicksAndRejections (node:internal/process/task_queues:90:21) {
  code: 'EADDRINUSE',
  errno: -48,
  syscall: 'listen',
  address: '::',
  port: 8090
}

Node.js v26.13.0

Child exit: 1 signal: null
```

After output:

```text
ai: /Users/gr2m/.codex/worktrees/375b/ai/packages/ai/dist/index.js
mcp (replaced in this isolated check): /Users/gr2m/.codex/worktrees/375b/ai/packages/mcp/dist/index.js
route: a6860a687011dbf025388ee419db730e05fb9ce0
POST statuses: [ 200, 200 ]
Consent responses: [ true, true ]


Child exit: 0 signal: null
```

The child process isolates the original unhandled bind failure. The
authorization function alone is substituted to create a pending consent
flow: no discovery, token exchange, MCP server request, model request,
or live provider login is performed. This is integration verification,
not a live-provider end-to-end result.

For the real HTTP smoke check, build the additional instrumentation
dependency and start the development app:

```sh
pnpm exec turbo build --filter=ai... --filter=@ai-sdk/openai... --filter=@ai-sdk/mcp... --filter=@ai-sdk/otel...
cd examples/ai-e2e-next
pnpm exec next dev --webpack --hostname 127.0.0.1 --port 3199
```

In another terminal:

```sh
node --input-type=module <<'JS'
const url = 'http://127.0.0.1:3199/api/chat/mcp-with-auth';
const responses = await Promise.all([0, 1].map(() => fetch(url, {
  method: 'POST',
  body: JSON.stringify({ messages: [] }),
  headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json', origin: 'http://127.0.0.1:3199' },
})));
console.log('Real Next.js anonymous concurrent POST:', responses.map(r => r.status));
console.log('Session route after requests:', (await fetch(url)).status);
JS
```

Actual result:

```text
Real Next.js anonymous concurrent POST: [ 401, 401 ]
Session route after requests: 200
```

The actual Next.js HTTP route rejects requests without a session and
remains responsive. Full live OAuth consent and chat generation were not
exercised: verification was restricted to local execution, with no
third-party security probes or account authorization. Initial startup
required building `@ai-sdk/otel` and restarting webpack after Turbopack
retained the missing-module diagnostic; the successful HTTP result above
is from the restarted app.

</details>

## Validation and review

- `pnpm --filter @example/next-openai test:mcp-auth`: 8 tests passed
after resolving the script conflict against current main.
- `pnpm --filter @example/next-openai test:mcp-elicitation`: 5 tests
passed; both test commands are preserved.
- `pnpm check`: passed, no lint warnings or errors.
- `pnpm discover-guidelines --modified`: no applicable guidelines.
- `pnpm run-verifiers --modified`: no applicable verifiers.
- `pnpm type-check:full`: passed on the resolved branch after rebuilding
workspace packages; CI TypeScript also passed. Initial local setup
required `pnpm --filter @example/nuxt-openai exec nuxt prepare`.
- Independent Claude Code Opus 5.5 review (`claude-opus-5-5`, model
confirmed by result metadata): no actionable findings for
`dc47f71efac5b93d8e38070a7f9655df4ddfa832`. No review-fix commits were
needed. The reviewer saw the initial Nuxt setup failure; the subsequent
full type check passed without source changes.
- CI: all 53 non-Agent checks passed for conflict-resolution commit
`7dd142b6e79c850b95fe901d29e6d13ea6077546`. All required checks passed.
Vercel Agent Review is excluded from the merge gate as explicitly
requested for the admin merge.

## Checklist

- [x] All commits are signed (PRs with unsigned commits cannot be
merged)
- [x] Tests have been added / updated (for bug fixes / features)
- [ ] Documentation has been added / updated (for bug fixes / features)
- [ ] A _patch_ changeset for relevant packages has been added (for bug
fixes / features - run `pnpm changeset` in the project root)
- [x] I have reviewed this pull request (self-review)

No changeset is needed: only example tests, their runner
command/configuration, and CI change. The README already documents the
command.

## Related Issues

Security finding `01M6EGZM5EJ05ENYAMBYYK1H6F`; regression coverage for
#24690.

## Change scope

Production-source diff: **+0 / -0**. Raw Git added/deleted lines exclude
examples, tests, and CI/configuration. No files in `packages/ai/`,
`packages/provider/`, or `packages/provider-utils/` changed.

