commit.message:
fix(provider-utils): reject HTTPS download downgrades (#24680)

## Background

Validated downloads could follow an HTTPS-to-HTTP redirect and fetch the
result over an insecure connection. Existing cross-origin credential
stripping remains effective, but does not prevent the transport
downgrade. Integrations that intentionally redirected from HTTPS to
HTTP, including a configured self-hosted target, now receive
`DownloadError`; they must keep the redirect chain on HTTPS or
explicitly start on HTTP.

## Summary

Reject HTTPS-to-HTTP redirects before contacting the target, even when
it matches `trustedOrigin` or the chain initially started on HTTP. Keep
initial HTTP requests, HTTP-to-HTTP redirects, HTTPS redirects, and
HTTP-to-HTTPS upgrades working. Add coverage for all five redirect
status codes, response-body cancellation, and trusted-origin handling,
plus documentation and a patch changeset. Cover private-address
rejection and HTTPS downgrade rejection independently in both MCP OAuth
discovery flows. Keep private-address redirect regressions in downloads,
`getFromApi`, and compatible image downloads on HTTPS so the downgrade
guard cannot mask them.

## End-to-End Verification

The same script exercises the exported `fetchWithValidatedRedirects` API
against local HTTP/HTTPS servers before and after rebuilding this
checkout's workspace package. An injected transport routes fixture
origins exclusively to loopback servers; the servers record whether
dummy authentication headers reached each hop.

<details>
<summary>Reproduction code, setup, and before/after results</summary>

Prerequisites: a supported Node.js version, pnpm 12, OpenSSL, and
installed workspace dependencies. No provider credentials are needed.
The temporary certificate is trusted only for this Node process using
`NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS`; TLS verification remains enabled.

Save the following as `/tmp/ai-sdk-redirect-fix/reproduce.mjs` (outside
the checkout):

```js
import { createServer as createHttpServer } from 'node:http';
import { createServer as createHttpsServer } from 'node:https';
import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';
import { fetchWithValidatedRedirects } from '@ai-sdk/provider-utils';

console.log('local package:', import.meta.resolve('@ai-sdk/provider-utils'));
const tls = {
  key: readFileSync('/tmp/ai-sdk-redirect-fix/key.pem'),
  cert: readFileSync('/tmp/ai-sdk-redirect-fix/cert.pem'),
};
const requests = [];
const handler = (req, res) => {
  requests.push({
    path: req.url,
    authorization: Boolean(req.headers.authorization),
    customKey: Boolean(req.headers['x-provider-key']),
    cookie: Boolean(req.headers.cookie),
    proxyAuthorization: Boolean(req.headers['proxy-authorization']),
  });
  const locations = {
    '/same': '/done',
    '/cross': 'https://cdn.example.net/back',
    '/back': 'https://api.example.com/done',
    '/downgrade': 'http://cdn.example.net/done',
    '/upgrade': 'https://api.example.com/downgrade',
  };
  if (locations[req.url]) {
    res.writeHead(302, { location: locations[req.url] });
    res.end('redirect');
  } else {
    res.end('download');
  }
};
const servers = [createHttpsServer(tls, handler), createHttpsServer(tls, handler), createHttpServer(handler)];
try {
  for (const server of servers) {
    await new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
      server.once('error', reject);
      server.listen(0, '127.0.0.1', resolve);
    });
  }
  const destinations = new Map([
    ['https://api.example.com', `https://localhost:${servers[0].address().port}`],
    ['https://cdn.example.net', `https://localhost:${servers[1].address().port}`],
    ['http://cdn.example.net', `http://127.0.0.1:${servers[2].address().port}`],
  ]);
  // This injected transport only contacts the loopback fixture servers.
  const localFetch = (input, init) => {
    const url = new URL(input);
    const destination = destinations.get(url.origin);
    if (!destination) throw new Error('Unexpected fixture origin');
    return fetch(new URL(url.pathname + url.search, destination), init);
  };
  for (const [scenario, url] of [
    ['same origin', 'https://api.example.com/same'],
    ['cross origin and return', 'https://api.example.com/cross'],
    ['HTTPS downgrade', 'https://api.example.com/downgrade'],
    ['HTTP upgrade then downgrade', 'http://cdn.example.net/upgrade'],
    ['initial HTTP', 'http://cdn.example.net/done'],
  ]) {
    requests.length = 0;
    try {
      const response = await fetchWithValidatedRedirects({
        url,
        headers: {
          Authorization: 'Bearer local-fixture',
          'X-Provider-Key': 'local-fixture',
          Cookie: 'session=local-fixture',
          'Proxy-Authorization': 'Basic local-fixture',
        },
        fetch: localFetch,
      });
      console.log(scenario, 'completed:', await response.text());
    } catch (error) {
      console.log(scenario, 'blocked:', error.name, error.message);
    }
    console.log(JSON.stringify(requests));
  }
} finally {
  await Promise.all(servers.map(server => new Promise(resolve => {
    server.close(resolve);
    server.closeAllConnections();
  })));
}
